{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917340298},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me break down what I need to do:\n\n1. I have two data sources:\n   - Farmers markets by state: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n   - US Census population data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\n2. I need to calculate: total farmers markets per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places\n\n3. According to the instructions, I should:\n   - First check if semantic models exist in the catalog\n   - Check if there are existing aliases\n   - Only if nothing exists, ingest the data\n   - Use xorq_select to compute values\n   - Use xorq_verify to verify the result\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for any existing semantic models or aliases."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GtVpdkvVwU455WkBAUauVK","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_016GhDvQNHsdBRvM276Jwr1c","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":367,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8310,"totalTokens":8687,"cost":{"inpu